let's face it Red Dead 2 has too many  things to do  you can barely step foot in the game  without being pulled in a million  different directions  it's a neurotics nightmare I'm telling  you but for those who'd rather simply  explore the land take in the sights and  maybe even discover a couple secrets  along the way we've got just the thing  for you now keep in mind  nobody likes spoiled eggs so if you'd  rather hunt for these on your own  what the hell are you doing here stop  watching this video and maybe check out  our let's play series dirty arty instead  okay here are seven of the best Easter  eggs we found so far in Red Dead  Redemption tube now as you might  remember from John Marston his time in  new Austin  swimming was a little bit dangerous to  say the least and Rockstar is very well  aware of that as they added a line of  dialogue poking fun at marcin's aversion  to water can't swim kids no more  thankfully Red Dead Redemption 2 allows  you to swim but Arthur isn't about to  let us forget about what we had to go  through in the first game there are a  number of Fantasy references in the game  including one that pays tribute to one  of our favorite junior our Tolkien  characters hobbits up in the hills near  Donner Falls you'll find a little  hillside home that looks very much like  the ones in lore of the Rings sadly  there are no hobbitses in sight but  Arthur will sketch out the house in his  journal leave him to ponder who might be  living there also there's a painting on  the back that looks like a turtle or  maybe a UFO yes you heard me we are not  alone in this universe but that's not to  say we didn't see it coming if you head  over to this cabin near emerald ranch  you'll be greeted with a bunch of  rotting corpses and the letter  explaining their otherworldly reasons  for drinking the home unbranded  non-carbonated fruit flavored soft drink  so to speak but all you have to do is  come back at 2 a.m. to catch a glimpse  of a hovering UFO if you want an even  better look at the spacecraft head on up  to the peak of Mount Shan and directly  after seeing the green glow in the cabin  and wait till 1:00 a.m. the next day  don't forget to snap a photo while  you're up there  are the UFOs part of a bigger mystery or  are they just another tiny footnote in  the game of densely packed world we'll  let you decide on that one speaking of  mysteries players spent years searching  for Bigfoot in the GTA series but in Red  Dead 2 he's right under our noses well  at least we think so if you're still  atop Mount Shan searching for UFOs you  can also find some bones of some kind of  giant tucked away in the corner of the  peak this may seem a little  disappointing to some if you're to  believe these belong to the famous  sasquatch but hold on there's more way  up north at the Calumet ravine visit the  spot right here then make your way over  to this mysterious cavern tucked away in  the mountains who's in there you might  wonder well why don't we just ask is  that so is it the legendary Bigfoot  maybe the Sasquatch from undead  nightmare or maybe it's just a super  insecure guy with a pituitary gland  problem whoever the mystery voice  belongs to we only really know that he's  a large man all right mr. big man it was  nice chatting with you and all but we've  gotta get going there is a ghost that  needs our attention wait what ghosts yes  there are some very haunted spirits  lurking in the mists deep in the Lemoine  swamps if you head up the Kumasi river  and near the border of New Hanover you  might hear a spooky voice calling that's  Agnes Dowd Agnes seems to have some  unfinished business as her dialogue  tells a somber tale of love and  heartache if you're in the mood for  sadness you can visit her every two days  in the swamps but she'll only appear if  it's a particularly foggy night so try  to get there between 10:00 p.m. and 4:00  a.m.  after she finishes telling her tale  she's gone forever so don't miss it now  if you're on the hunt for more sad  Easter eggs here's one more just south  the flat next station in the heartland  there's a corpse washed up on the beach  but try and Luda and whoa this one's  still alive as it turns out the dying  man appears to be the former lover of  Bonnie McFarlane whom you might remember  as the farmhand from Red Dead one that  helps John out early on in the game the  letter he hands you talks of him and  Bonnie destined for each other that  they're meant to be together raising  kids and that he's determined to make a  fortune and set things straight between  them unfortunately as you can tell that  never happens  his final resting spot is not on the bed  with Bonnie by his side but rather on  the beach broke disheveled and alone  sorry to bum you all out with that  Easter egg um how about we end on the  fun one okay so we've established that  aliens exist so there's got to be other  extraterrestrial happenings in the game  right well if you make your way over to  Roanoke Valley in northern and this burg  you can find remnants of a meteor crash  the family living in the home where it  landed certainly won't mind you snooping  around as they're all kind of dead at  the moment so feel free to check out the  space rock for yourself and maybe even  bring home a souvenir or two so those  were just some of the many many Easter  eggs hidden in the far corners of Red  Dead Redemption twos map if you found  one that people need to know about leave  it in the comments below and we might  get to it in a future video until then  though happy hunting and don't forget to  check out gamespot.com  for more Red Dead Redemption 2 features  and guides thanks for watching  you
 

